  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"535\" data-end=\"607\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"535\" data-end=\"549\">Method:</strong></span><br data-start=\"549\" data-end=\"552\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">MLPA (Multiplex Ligation-dependent Probe Amplification)</span></p>\n<p data-start=\"609\" data-end=\"633\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"609\" data-end=\"631\">&nbsp;Interpretation:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"634\" data-end=\"1104\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"634\" data-end=\"728\">\n<p data-start=\"636\" data-end=\"728\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Detects <strong data-start=\"644\" data-end=\"679\">large deletions or duplications</strong> in genes associated with <strong data-start=\"705\" data-end=\"727\">hereditary cancers</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"729\" data-end=\"839\">\n<p data-start=\"731\" data-end=\"839\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Covers <strong data-start=\"738\" data-end=\"750\">30 genes</strong> linked to cancers such as <strong data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"833\">breast, ovarian, colorectal, pancreatic, endometrial</strong>, etc.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"840\" data-end=\"925\">\n<p data-start=\"842\" data-end=\"925\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Used when sequencing does not detect mutations but clinical suspicion remains high.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"926\" data-end=\"1021\">\n<p data-start=\"928\" data-end=\"1021\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Helps in <strong data-start=\"937\" data-end=\"959\">genetic counseling</strong>, <strong data-start=\"961\" data-end=\"989\">screening family members</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"995\" data-end=\"1020\">tailored surveillance</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1022\" data-end=\"1104\">\n<p data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1104\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">A <strong data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1045\">positive result</strong> may require further confirmation and genetic consultation.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
